(subclass ExpectedBehaviorViolationBug SoftwareBug)
(termFormat EnglishLanguage ExpectedBehaviorViolationBug "expected behavior violation bug")
(documentation ExpectedBehaviorViolationBug EnglishLanguage "A &%SoftwareBug
whose discriminating property is that a &%Specification recording the
&%intendedBehavior was articulated by the specifying agent prior to the
deviation, and a &%Document (or other &%ContentBearingObject) records that
&%Specification via &%containsInformation.  Adapted from CWE-440 (Expected
Behavior Violation) : 'A feature, API, or function does not perform according
to its specification.'")

(=>
  (and
    (instance ?PROG ComputerProgram)
    (programBehavior ?PROG ?INPUT ?ACTUAL)
    (intendedBehavior ?PROG ?INTENDED ?AGENT)
    (not (equal ?ACTUAL ?INTENDED))
    (not (instance ?ACTUAL ?INTENDED))
    (exists (?SPEC ?DOC ?DECL)
      (and
        (instance ?SPEC Specification)
        (instance ?DOC ContentBearingObject)
        (containsInformation ?DOC ?SPEC)
        (instance ?DECL Declaring)
        (agent ?DECL ?AGENT)
        (patient ?DECL ?SPEC))))
  (exists (?BUG)
    (and
      (instance ?BUG ExpectedBehaviorViolationBug)
      (bugInProgram ?BUG ?PROG ?AGENT))))

